Parity note: PageSkeleton.tsx is a pure presentational set of shaped skeleton blocks with no
data fetch. The generic state matrix lists loading/empty/error/stale/offline, but this surface
*is* the loading representation and the web source has no error/stale/offline branch of its own —
those are what the skeleton stands in FOR (a host shows PageSkeleton while loading, then swaps to
content/EmptyState/QueryError). All four web building blocks are reproduced; the one branch this
surface owns — an empty plan — renders a guarded fallback skeleton, never a blank box. This mirrors
the accepted precedent of feature-views/SummaryStatsRow (a presentational leaf that reproduces only
the web branches and documents that lifecycle chrome is owned by the host).

